---
description: Scoped NGINX CVE predicates and advisory maintenance
globs: gixy/plugins/_nginx_cves*.py,tests/plugins/test_nginx_cves*.py,docs/{en,ru,zh}/checks/nginx-cves.md
alwaysApply: false
---

- @gixy/plugins/_nginx_cves_db.py owns OSS intervals;
  @gixy/plugins/_nginx_cves_november.py owns November configuration predicates;
  use nginx.org for historical OSS bounds and F5 CNA records for prerequisites.
- Evaluate effective settings within their HTTP, mail or stream protocol roots.
  Never combine sibling locations or unrelated servers; retain all active
  same-scope logs. Stream settings inherit only from their stream ancestor.
- Select stream default servers per listen address/port, honoring explicit
  `default_server` and otherwise the first server on that listener. Respect
  nearer overrides, explicit `off`, and version-dependent TLS defaults.
- November 2026 adds ten F5 CNA prerequisites, bringing coverage to 73 of 77
  official CVE IDs (74 of 78 with CVE-2026-132779). Nine fixes are 1.30.7/1.31.9; CVE-2026-120993 affects only
  mainline 1.31.4-1.31.8 and is fixed in 1.31.9. Keep the four exclusions.
- CVE-2026-132779 (23 Nov 2026) brings coverage to 74 of 78 official IDs; fixed
  1.30.8/1.31.10. Prerequisite: effective `ssl_early_data on` on an HTTP TLS 1.3
  server (shares `_tls13_listeners` with CVE-2026-118899); mitigation `off`.
- Keep resolver subrequest checks, regex-map/try_files captures and dynamic
  certificates lexical and bounded. Never claim request-time hostname equality,
  connection exhaustion or exploitability from static prerequisite matches.
- Reuse lexical variable helpers; do not execute supplied regexes or add a general
  variable-flow engine. Keep legacy shared HTTP/3 predicates stable.
- @tests/plugins/test_nginx_cves_october_scopes.py and
  @tests/plugins/test_nginx_cves_november.py exercise real parser/auditor
  prerequisites, overrides, anchors, counts and stable/mainline fix boundaries.
- @docs/en/checks/nginx-cves.md and its Russian/Chinese translations must
  distinguish version advice and prerequisites
  from exploit proof, document exclusions and arbitrary-indirection limitations.
